    {
      "id": "claim_4a19ed4b2d5d4f1b8dcd027905575000",
      "statement": "Local services may remain unconfigured without bypassing Pro checks, but the manual Build workflow requires release service and signing configuration in the app-store-connect environment. It validates version/platform inputs, skips submodules, avoids canceling in-progress runs, validates Firebase and public Apple RevenueCat settings, installs ignored temporary service files with symbol upload enabled, and schedules cleanup even on failure. Configuration-bearing logs and private build directories must not be published. Its apple-build contract tests cover input and service rejection and export options, not actual upload or Sandbox purchases.",
      "evidence": [
